sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2025-wisdom-01> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Planaria, despite chaotic mixoploid genomes from ~400 million years of asexual reproduction and large numbers of plastic proliferative stem cells, are champions of regeneration, cancer resistant and apparently do not age, the opposite of what a 'genome drives function' paradigm would predict.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Planaria have chaotic genomes yet regenerate, resist cancer and do not age";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “The Multiscale Wisdom of the Body: Collective Intelligence as a Tractable Interface for Next-Generation Biomedicine”, BioEssays : news and reviews in molecular, cellular and developmental biology (2025), doi:10.1002/bies.202400196; section “Introduction”. Scope: Asexual planarian flatworms (e.g. Schmidtea mediterranea asexual strain)"
}
